description:
Lesson 5.02 ran an experiment on the standard rounding functions. Use what it found, and their reference pages, to write four functions with exactly these behaviours. Run your own small experiment first if any row surprises you.

```cpp-norun
double roundHalfAway(double x);
double roundHalfEven(double x);
double towardZero(double x);
std::optional<int> toIntChecked(double x);
```

| Function | Rounds to the nearest whole number, and halves go ... | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| `roundHalfAway` | away from zero | 2.5 → 3, -2.5 → -3, 0.5 → 1 |
| `roundHalfEven` | to the even neighbour | 2.5 → 2, 3.5 → 4, -2.5 → -2, 0.5 → 0 |
| `towardZero` | (no rounding: drops the fraction) | 2.9 → 2, -2.9 → -2 |

**toIntChecked** drops the fraction like `towardZero` and returns the result as an `int`, or an empty optional if `x` is NaN, infinite, or the result does not fit in an `int`. (Converting such a value with `static_cast<int>` is undefined behaviour, which is why this function exists.)

starter.solution.cpp:
#include <optional>

double roundHalfAway(double x) { return x; }
double roundHalfEven(double x) { return x; }
double towardZero(double x) { return x; }
std::optional<int> toIntChecked(double x) { return std::nullopt; }

solution.solution.cpp:
#include <climits>
#include <cmath>
#include <optional>

double roundHalfAway(double x) { return std::round(x); }
double roundHalfEven(double x) { return std::nearbyint(x); }
double towardZero(double x) { return std::trunc(x); }

std::optional<int> toIntChecked(double x)
{
    if (!std::isfinite(x)) return std::nullopt;
    const double t{ std::trunc(x) };
    if (t < static_cast<double>(INT_MIN) || t > static_cast<double>(INT_MAX)) return std::nullopt;
    return static_cast<int>(t);
}

unitTests:
#include <limits>
TEST("halves away from zero") {
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfAway(2.5), 3, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfAway(-2.5), -3, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfAway(0.5), 1, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfAway(2.4999), 2, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfAway(-7.6), -8, 0);
}
TEST("halves to even") {
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfEven(2.5), 2, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfEven(3.5), 4, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfEven(-2.5), -2, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfEven(0.5), 0, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfEven(1.5), 2, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(roundHalfEven(2.6), 3, 0);
}
TEST("dropping the fraction") {
    CHECK_NEAR(towardZero(2.9), 2, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(towardZero(-2.9), -2, 0);
    CHECK_NEAR(towardZero(5), 5, 0);
}
TEST("checked conversion to int") {
    CHECK(toIntChecked(3.99) == std::optional<int>{ 3 });
    CHECK(toIntChecked(-3.99) == std::optional<int>{ -3 });
    CHECK(toIntChecked(2147483647.9) == std::optional<int>{ 2147483647 });
    CHECK(toIntChecked(-2147483648.7) == std::optional<int>{ -2147483647 - 1 });
    CHECK(!toIntChecked(2147483648.0).has_value());
    CHECK(!toIntChecked(-2147483649.0).has_value());
    CHECK(!toIntChecked(1e300).has_value());
    CHECK(!toIntChecked(std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()).has_value());
    CHECK(!toIntChecked(-std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity()).has_value());
}

